What are Subsurface Drip Irrigation Pipes?
Subsurface drip irrigation pipes represent an advanced agricultural water delivery technology buried 30-50 centimeters beneath the soil surface. Constructed from durable, corrosion-resistant materials like polyethylene (PE) and polyvinyl chloride (PVC), these systems deliver water and nutrients directly to plant root zones with precision. Their underground positioning provides significant advantages over traditional irrigation methods—reducing evaporation losses by up to 50% while minimizing human or equipment-induced damage. When integrated with modern control systems, they form the backbone of water-efficient precision agriculture.

